# Diagram Format Standards

Standards for creating and formatting diagrams in documentation.

<rule>
name: mermaid_diagram_format
description: Standardizes all diagrams to use Mermaid format for consistency and maintainability
filters:
  # Match any Markdown files
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.md$"
  # Match content that looks like a diagram
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?s)```(?!mermaid).*?(?:┌|┐|└|┘|│|─|┬|┴|┼|←|→|↑|↓).*?```"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      All diagrams in documentation should use Mermaid format instead of ASCII art or other formats.
      
      Convert diagrams to Mermaid format using the appropriate diagram type:
      
      ```mermaid
      flowchart TD
          A[Start] --> B{Decision}
          B -->|Yes| C[Process]
          B -->|No| D[End]
      ```
      
      Common diagram types:
      - flowchart (TD for top-down, LR for left-right)
      - sequenceDiagram
      - classDiagram
      - stateDiagram-v2
      - entityRelationshipDiagram
      - gantt
      
      For more information, visit the [Mermaid documentation](https://mermaid-js.github.io/mermaid/#/).

examples:
  - input: |
      ```
      ┌─────┐     ┌─────┐
      │  A  │---->│  B  │
      └─────┘     └─────┘
      ```
    output: |
      ```mermaid
      flowchart LR
          A --> B
      ```

metadata:
  priority: medium
  version: 1.0
</rule>